+						    *socketserver-security*
+WARNING: A TCP socketserver has no access control.  Any process on the same
+machine, including those of other users, can connect to the port and send
+keys or expressions, which allows executing arbitrary commands as the user
+running the Vim server.  Only use a TCP address in a trusted, single-user
+environment.  On Unix, prefer a socket path or name (see |socketserver-name|),
+which is protected by file permissions.
+
 						    *socketserver-differences*
